# RingCentral Integration

- Scope this work to `vantage-main-server`. Runtime RingCentral code lives in `src/services/ringcentral/`; diagnostics and manual runners live in `scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/`.
- Use native `fetch` only. Do not add Axios or RingCentral SDKs unless explicitly requested.
- Env is loaded by package scripts with `node --env-file=.env ./node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs ...`. Run commands with `pnpm` from `vantage-main-server`.
- Required env vars: `RC_SERVER_URL`, `RC_CLIENT_ID`, `RC_CLIENT_SECRET`, `RC_JWT`. Use `getRequiredEnv()` from `src/config/domain` in runtime/service code.
- Never log or commit `RC_JWT`, `RC_CLIENT_SECRET`, OAuth access tokens, refresh tokens, or Authorization headers.

## Runtime Service Boundaries

- `ringcentral-config.ts` owns all RingCentral env toggles, collection names, collection mode, duplicate window, cron lookback/overlap, analytics buffer, and lead write mode.
- `RINGCENTRAL_GRANOT_ADOPTION_ENABLED` is a narrow fail-closed gate, default false. Enabled convergence still mutates Leads only when the existing RingCentral write mode is `create`; shadow/dry-run remain non-mutating for adoption/conflict.
- `client.ts`, `auth.ts`, and token stores own RingCentral API access. Keep token persistence storage-agnostic through `TokenStore`.
- The Operations Registry RingCentral route snapshot owns inbound-number identity and attribution. `call-lead-sources.ts` is migration/test seed data only; runtime code must not import it or fall back to it.
- Webhook flow: capture raw events, normalize party events, upsert candidates, aggregate sessions, then call shared ingest only when the session is qualified and terminal.
- Cron flow: `call-log-sync.service.ts` claims the Mongo state lease, fetches detailed inbound Call Log records page by page, `call-log-vetting.ts` qualifies them, then shared ingest handles idempotency/duplicates/write mode.
- `call-log-sync-state.store.ts` alone owns the singleton `key:"account"` cursor and its five-minute renewable lease. A cron request is only a trigger; Mongo elects the winner. Provider responses, process memory, Vercel overlap assumptions, and logs are not coordination authority. Never add a local lock, spin, or wait.
- Claim filter is `key = "account" AND (leased_until missing OR <= now)`. Every renewal and terminal write is fenced by `{ key, lease_owner, leased_until: { $gt: now } }`, so a stale owner cannot renew, finalize, clear, or overwrite a successor. Expiry is the only recovery; a terminated process needs no cleanup.
- `lastSyncFrom`/`lastSyncTo` move only in the fenced full-success update. Pagination, throttle, vetting/route, adoption/conflict/ledger, normal-ingest, lease-loss, and terminal-write failures all leave the cursor untouched. Never advance per page or per record, and never treat partial completion as success.
- The 12-hour `RINGCENTRAL_CALL_LOG_SYNC_ROLLING_LOOKBACK_MINUTES` floor is locked and independent of the cron cadence. Do not shrink it when changing the schedule; repeated scans are safe through processed-call/adoption idempotency.
- Persist bounded run telemetry only: `last_runtime_ms`, `last_adopted_count`, `last_adoption_conflict_count`, `last_throttled_count`, and a `lastError` code from the closed set in `call-log-sync-state.store.ts`. Emit `ringcentral_call_log_runtime_ms`, `ringcentral_adoptions_total{outcome}`, and `ringcentral_call_log_lease_contention_total` from `ringcentral-metrics.ts`, plus PII-safe `started`/`completed`/`failed`/`lease_contended`/`lease_recovered`/`lease_lost` events carrying a masked owner hash only.
- The Call Log cron route maps contention to `{ ok: true, skipped: true, reason: "lease_held" }`. Normal overlap is never HTTP 500, and a genuine failure returns a bounded non-sensitive body.
- Analytics flow: `analytics-reconcile.service.ts` stores aggregate snapshots only. It must not create caller-level leads.
- `ringcentral-call-lead-ingest.service.ts` is the only RingCentral promotion gate. Its order is processed-call idempotency, optional Granot-created Lead convergence, business duplicate classification, then create/shadow/dry-run only when adoption did not succeed. Real creates persist top-level `ingestion_origin=ringcentral`; adoption preserves `ingestion_origin=granot_lead_created`. Nested `ringcentral.ingestion_source` remains webhook/call-log/manual transport provenance.
- `callLeadConvergence.service.ts` alone owns candidate selection and canonical adoption/conflict. Routes, webhook/session code, Call Log sync, clients, and the duplicate guard must not select or mutate candidates.
- Granot Call creation and RingCentral adoption/normal creation must acquire the same hashed Granularity+phone convergence scope fence before checking or creating. Keep raw phones out of lock rows, and recover revision/idempotency races by re-reading ledger/candidates rather than failing or creating a second Lead.

## Safety Posture

- Default posture is dry-run. Real lead creation requires `RINGCENTRAL_CREATE_CALL_LEADS=true`; shadow creation requires `RINGCENTRAL_SHADOW_CALL_LEADS=true` with real creation off.
- Roll adoption out independently: verify the processed-call session and call-log identity fences, keep `RINGCENTRAL_GRANOT_ADOPTION_ENABLED=false` until separately approved, and preserve the existing create/shadow/dry-run posture. Roll back by disabling adoption first; never detach committed caller/telephony evidence, reset convergence, delete conflict/ledger/Command/Change/outbox evidence, or automatically reverse duplicate classification.
- The Call Log run requires the unique `{ key: 1 }` index `ringcentral_call_log_sync_state_key_unique`; it is the fail-closed mechanism that keeps a first-run race from creating two singleton rows. Runtime never creates it and refuses to run without it. Deploy through `pnpm migration:granot-lifecycle:indexes -- --report | --apply --confirm-production=<db> | --verify`; report/verify are read-only, apply requires separate authorization, and multiple `account` rows must be reported rather than merged or deleted.
- Adoption requires unique sparse `telephonySessionId` and `callLogId` indexes on `ringcentral_processed_calls`. Runtime transaction paths do not create indexes. `migration:ringcentral:processed-call-indexes` is report-first, refuses collisions, and requires explicit database/apply authorization plus matching collection mode. Unit 20 added this utility but did not authorize or perform a production apply.
- Token storage may use Mongo via `RC_TOKEN_STORE=mongo`; local file cache `.ringcentral-token-cache.json` remains supported and ignored by git.
- RingCentral collection names are mode-aware. Confirm `RINGCENTRAL_COLLECTION_MODE` before touching production state.
- Manual runners live under `scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/`. There are **no** `pnpm ringcentral:*` scripts in `package.json`. Invoke with `node --env-file=.env ./node_modules/tsx/dist/cli.mjs scripts/dev_ops/ringcentral/<script>.ts` (for example `ringcentral-diagnose.ts`, `ringcentral-webhook-create.ts`, `ringcentral-webhook-create-local.ts`, `ringcentral-webhook-monitor.ts`).
- RingCentral validation/probe outputs must stay sanitized and gitignored.

## Auth Flow

- JWT exchange: `POST ${RC_SERVER_URL}/restapi/oauth/token` with Basic auth for `RC_CLIENT_ID:RC_CLIENT_SECRET` and form body `grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer&assertion=${RC_JWT}`.
- Refresh flow uses the same token endpoint with `grant_type=refresh_token`.
- Token rules: use cached access token if it expires more than 120s from now; otherwise refresh if refresh token is valid; if refresh fails, delete cache and exchange JWT; on API `401`, delete cache, exchange JWT, retry once.

## Access Model

- The JWT represents one RingCentral user/extension, not automatic org-wide access.
- Account-level analytics require `/restapi/v1.0/account/~/call-log?view=Detailed`; compare against `/restapi/v1.0/account/~/extension/~/call-log?view=Detailed`.
- Organization-level access is only proven when account-level logs work and returned records include multiple extensions or company numbers.

## Production Direction

- Production token storage should use `RC_TOKEN_STORE=mongo`, `connectMongo()` from `src/db.ts`, active DB via `getMongoDatabaseName()`/`MONGO_DATABASE_NAME`, collection `integration_tokens`, key `ringcentral:oauth-token`.
- API routes must never return token values. Cron routes require `CRON_SECRET`.
- The Call Log cron runs at `*/30 * * * *` in `vercel.json`. The cadence is the last change in any lease/cursor work and is never used to compensate for an unsafe cursor, a missing lease, a false duplicate, or a failing convergence test. Roll back by restoring `0 */2 * * *` first, then `RINGCENTRAL_CALL_LOG_SYNC_ENABLED=false`, then Unit 20's adoption flag if adoption is unsafe; keep the additive lease/telemetry fields and the unique safety index, and never rewind a successful cursor without a reviewed recovery plan.
- Before changing cron cadence, lead write flags, or mapped numbers, update the relevant tests/rules so docs match runtime behavior.
